{"id": "185320", "name": "התאמת נוסחאות של מסילות במישור לציורים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "functions": [{"name": "x1", "params": ["t"], "body": "x1"}, {"name": "y1", "params": ["t"], "body": "y1"}, {"name": "x2", "params": ["t"], "body": "x2"}, {"name": "y2", "params": ["t"], "body": "y2"}, {"name": "x3", "params": ["t"], "body": "x3"}, {"name": "y3", "params": ["t"], "body": "y3"}, {"name": "r2", "params": ["v"], "body": "block([w:round(100*v)/100],if integerp(w) then w else float(w))"}], "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Match between the formulas of functions \\(\\alpha_i: [a,b] \\rightarrow R^2\\) and the paths (representing the images of these functions) depicted in the graphs below.</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:12px\"><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 1:</div>{{CT:0}}</div><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 2:</div>{{CT:1}}</div><div style=\"flex:0 1 360px;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:4px\">Graph 3:</div>{{CT:2}}</div></div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>(Please answer with 1, 2 or 3)</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\alpha_1(t)=({{CT:3}}, {{CT:4}})\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number: [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\alpha_2(t)=({{CT:5}}, {{CT:6}})\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number: [[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"></div><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\alpha_3(t)=({{CT:7}}, {{CT:8}})\\) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Graph number: [[input:ans3]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans3]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> A picture shows only the set of points the path passes through. To identify it, compute a few points of each path, at \\(t=0,\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\) and \\(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\), and look for the picture that passes through them in this order.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Points on each path</b><br>Substituting into each formula (at the first four values \\(\\sin\\) and \\(\\cos\\) take only the values \\(0,\\pm1\\); at \\(t=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\) both equal \\(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\approx0.71\\), and a cube makes them smaller, \\(\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\right)^3\\approx0.35\\)):<div style=\"overflow-x:auto;margin:8px 0\"><table dir=\"ltr\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:0 auto\"><tr style=\"background:#F4F1F5;color:#4b1f6f\"><th style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\"></th><th style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(t=0\\)</th><th style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\)</th><th style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(t=\\pi\\)</th><th style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(t=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\)</th><th style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(t=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\) (approx.)</th><th style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">Graph</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(\\alpha_1\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:9}},{{CT:10}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:11}},{{CT:12}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:13}},{{CT:14}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:15}},{{CT:16}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:17}},{{CT:18}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">{{CT:19}}</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(\\alpha_2\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:20}},{{CT:21}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:22}},{{CT:23}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:24}},{{CT:25}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:26}},{{CT:27}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:28}},{{CT:29}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">{{CT:30}}</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(\\alpha_3\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:31}},{{CT:32}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:33}},{{CT:34}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:35}},{{CT:36}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:37}},{{CT:38}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">\\(({{CT:39}},{{CT:40}})\\)</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D1DD;text-align:center\">{{CT:41}}</td></tr></table></div>The largest value of \\(|x|\\) and of \\(|y|\\) on each path is the coefficient in front of the corresponding function, so these points also show how far the picture extends along each axis. Two coordinates that are functions of the same \\(\\sin t\\) (or the same \\(\\cos t\\)) give an arc traced back and forth, while a \\(\\sin\\)/\\(\\cos\\) pair gives a closed curve around the origin.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The matching</b><br>Each picture passes through the points of exactly one row of the table (in this order as \\(t\\) grows), so<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\alpha_1:\\ {{CT:42}},\\qquad \\alpha_2:\\ {{CT:43}},\\qquad \\alpha_3:\\ {{CT:44}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br />[[feedback:prt2]]<br />[[feedback:prt3]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "sol1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The first match is incorrect, {{CT:19}} is the correct graph.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "sol2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The second match is incorrect, {{CT:30}} is the correct graph.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "sol3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is correct.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">The third match is incorrect, {{CT:41}} is the correct graph.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["lst", "lst1", "lst2", "lst3", "lst4", "lst5", "path_lst", "sol1", "sol2", "sol3", "x1", "x11", "x2", "x22", "x3", "x33", "y1", "y11", "y2", "y22", "y3", "y33"], "nvariants": 50}